- `action(n1, "start the process")`: Hallucinated payload; the source text does not describe an explicit action to start the process, as it begins directly with checking the Referee Reports.
- `action(n14, "End")`: Hallucinated payload; the text does not define a distinct "End" action step. Termination should solely be represented by the `end(e1)` node.
- `precedence(n2, b1)`: The model omits concurrent behavior. The text explicitly states, "At the same time, you should continue to monitor if the Referee Reports have been completed," which requires parallel execution (an AND branch), but the model strictly sequences a single check.
- `precedence(n4, c1)`: The model creates an unconditional flow from `n4` to `c1`, entirely omitting the decision gateway described in the text ("If they have, you can continue... If not..."). 
- `label(n4, c1, "Yes")`: This label implies a conditional "Yes" path, but it is incorrectly assigned to an unconditional sequence flow leaving an action node (`n4`) instead of a branch gateway.
- `action`: The model completely omits the behavior "flag it again and send another reminder" which the text explicitly requires if the second check of the Referee Reports reveals they are still not completed.